<html>
<head>
    <title>CorbitChat Administration</title>
    <meta name="decorator" content="atl.admin"/>
    <meta name="admin.active.section" content="admin_plugins_menu/jim-admin-section"/>
    <meta name="admin.active.tab" content="jim-admin-link"/>
</head>
<body>
<div id="jim-admin-page">
    <header class="jim-admin-header">
        <h1>CorbitChat Administration</h1>
        <p class="jim-admin-subtitle">Chat access, notifications, attachments and diagnostics for the CorbitChat messenger.</p>
    </header>

    <nav class="jim-admin-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Admin sections">
        <button type="button" class="jim-admin-tab is-active" data-tab="overview" role="tab" aria-selected="true">Overview</button>
        <button type="button" class="jim-admin-tab" data-tab="access" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Access Control</button>
        <button type="button" class="jim-admin-tab" data-tab="notifications" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Notifications</button>
        <button type="button" class="jim-admin-tab" data-tab="attachments" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Attachments</button>
        <button type="button" class="jim-admin-tab" data-tab="diagnostics" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Diagnostics</button>
        <button type="button" class="jim-admin-tab" data-tab="license" role="tab" aria-selected="false">License</button>
        <button type="button" class="jim-admin-tab" data-tab="help" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Help</button>
    </nav>

    <div id="jim-admin-message" class="jim-admin-message" role="alert" hidden></div>

    <!-- ===== Overview ===== -->
    <section class="jim-admin-panel is-active" data-panel="overview">
        <div id="jim-admin-overview-cards" class="jim-admin-cards">
            <div class="jim-admin-card"><div class="jim-admin-card-label">Chat mode</div><div class="jim-admin-card-value" data-overview="chatMode">...</div></div>
            <div class="jim-admin-card"><div class="jim-admin-card-label">Web push</div><div class="jim-admin-card-value" data-overview="pushEnabled">...</div></div>
            <div class="jim-admin-card"><div class="jim-admin-card-label">Attachments</div><div class="jim-admin-card-value" data-overview="attachmentsEnabled">...</div></div>
            <div class="jim-admin-card"><div class="jim-admin-card-label">Access policies</div><div class="jim-admin-card-value" data-overview="policyCount">...</div></div>
            <div class="jim-admin-card"><div class="jim-admin-card-label">Push subscriptions</div><div class="jim-admin-card-value" data-overview="pushSubscriptionCount">...</div></div>
            <div class="jim-admin-card"><div class="jim-admin-card-label">Plugin version</div><div class="jim-admin-card-value" data-overview="pluginVersion">...</div></div>
            <div class="jim-admin-card"><div class="jim-admin-card-label">License</div><div class="jim-admin-card-value" id="jim-overview-license">...</div></div>
        </div>
        <h3>Recent admin changes</h3>
        <div id="jim-admin-audit-list" class="jim-admin-audit-list">Loading...</div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== Access Control ===== -->
    <section class="jim-admin-panel" data-panel="access">
        <h3>Global chat mode</h3>
        <div class="jim-admin-field">
            <label class="jim-admin-radio"><input type="radio" name="jim-chat-mode" value="ALLOW_ALL"/> <strong>Allow everyone</strong> — every active Jira user can search and chat with anyone.</label>
            <label class="jim-admin-radio"><input type="radio" name="jim-chat-mode" value="RESTRICTED"/> <strong>Restricted by policy</strong> — only the rules below decide who can search, start and receive chats. No matching rule means no access.</label>
            <label class="jim-admin-radio"><input type="radio" name="jim-chat-mode" value="DISABLED"/> <strong>Disabled</strong> — chat is turned off for all users.</label>
            <button id="jim-save-chat-mode" type="button" class="aui-button aui-button-primary">Save chat mode</button>
        </div>

        <h3>Access policies</h3>
        <p class="jim-admin-hint">Highest priority wins; on a tie DENY overrides ALLOW. Policies only apply in <strong>Restricted by policy</strong> mode.</p>
        <table class="aui jim-admin-policy-table" id="jim-policy-table">
            <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Source</th><th>Target</th><th>Action</th>
                <th>Search</th><th>Start</th><th>Receive</th>
                <th>Enabled</th><th>Priority</th><th></th>
            </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="jim-policy-rows">
            <tr><td colspan="9">Loading...</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h4 id="jim-policy-form-title">Add policy</h4>
        <div class="jim-admin-policy-form" id="jim-policy-form">
            <select id="jim-pol-source-type"><option value="USER">USER</option><option value="GROUP">GROUP</option></select>
            <input id="jim-pol-source-value" type="text" placeholder="username or group name"/>
            <span class="jim-admin-arrow">&#8594;</span>
            <select id="jim-pol-target-type"><option value="ANY">ANY</option><option value="USER">USER</option><option value="GROUP">GROUP</option></select>
            <input id="jim-pol-target-value" type="text" placeholder="username or group name"/>
            <select id="jim-pol-action"><option value="ALLOW">ALLOW</option><option value="DENY">DENY</option></select>
            <label><input id="jim-pol-can-search" type="checkbox" checked/> search</label>
            <label><input id="jim-pol-can-start" type="checkbox" checked/> start</label>
            <label><input id="jim-pol-can-receive" type="checkbox" checked/> receive</label>
            <input id="jim-pol-priority" type="number" value="0" title="Priority"/>
            <button id="jim-pol-add" type="button" class="aui-button">Add policy</button>
            <button id="jim-pol-cancel-edit" type="button" class="aui-button aui-button-link" hidden>Cancel</button>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== Notifications ===== -->
    <section class="jim-admin-panel" data-panel="notifications">
        <h3>Notification settings</h3>
        <div class="jim-admin-field">
            <label class="jim-admin-check"><input type="checkbox" id="jim-set-enableWebPush"/> Enable web push notifications</label>
            <label class="jim-admin-label" for="jim-set-notificationDetailLevel">Notification detail level</label>
            <select id="jim-set-notificationDetailLevel">
                <option value="FULL_MESSAGE">Full message — sender and message excerpt</option>
                <option value="SENDER_ONLY">Sender only — sender name, generic body</option>
                <option value="GENERIC_ONLY">Generic only — no sender, no content</option>
            </select>
            <label class="jim-admin-check"><input type="checkbox" id="jim-set-aggregateNotifications"/> Aggregate notifications (one notification replaces the previous instead of stacking)</label>
            <label class="jim-admin-check"><input type="checkbox" id="jim-set-mentionNotifications"/> Push notifications for @mentions</label>
            <label class="jim-admin-check"><input type="checkbox" id="jim-set-assignmentNotifications"/> Push notifications for issue assignments</label>
            <div class="jim-admin-actions">
                <button id="jim-save-notifications" type="button" class="aui-button aui-button-primary">Save notification settings</button>
                <button id="jim-test-notification" type="button" class="aui-button">Send test notification to me</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== Attachments ===== -->
    <section class="jim-admin-panel" data-panel="attachments">
        <h3>Attachment settings</h3>
        <div class="jim-admin-field">
            <label class="jim-admin-check"><input type="checkbox" id="jim-set-attachmentsEnabled"/> Allow file and voice attachments</label>
            <label class="jim-admin-label" for="jim-set-maxAttachmentSizeMb">Maximum attachment size (MB, 1&#8211;100)</label>
            <input type="number" id="jim-set-maxAttachmentSizeMb" min="1" max="100"/>
            <label class="jim-admin-label" for="jim-set-allowedExtensions">Allowed extensions (comma separated, e.g. <code>png,jpg,pdf</code>; empty = built-in safe list)</label>
            <input type="text" id="jim-set-allowedExtensions" placeholder="png,jpg,pdf"/>
            <label class="jim-admin-check"><input type="checkbox" id="jim-set-imagePreviewEnabled"/> Show inline image previews in chat</label>
            <div class="jim-admin-actions">
                <button id="jim-save-attachments" type="button" class="aui-button aui-button-primary">Save attachment settings</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== Diagnostics ===== -->
    <section class="jim-admin-panel" data-panel="diagnostics">
        <h3>Diagnostics</h3>
        <table class="aui jim-admin-diag-table">
            <tbody id="jim-diag-rows">
            <tr><td colspan="2">Loading...</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        <button id="jim-diag-refresh" type="button" class="aui-button">Refresh</button>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== License ===== -->
    <section class="jim-admin-panel" data-panel="license">
        <h3>Marketplace license</h3>
        <div id="jim-license-state-banner" class="jim-admin-license-banner" hidden></div>
        <table class="aui jim-admin-diag-table">
            <tbody id="jim-license-rows">
            <tr><td colspan="2">Loading...</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        <button id="jim-license-refresh" type="button" class="aui-button">Refresh</button>
        <div class="jim-admin-help" style="margin-top: 16px;">
            <h4>Managing the license</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Licenses are purchased and managed through Atlassian Marketplace; CorbitChat does not handle billing itself.</li>
                <li>To install or update a license go to <strong>Administration &rarr; Manage apps</strong>, expand <strong>CorbitChat</strong> and paste the license key into the <strong>License key</strong> field.</li>
                <li>While the license is missing or expired, sending messages, creating conversations, user search, attachments, push notifications and admin configuration changes are blocked. Existing conversations stay readable and this admin overview remains accessible.</li>
                <li>The raw license key is never displayed here, returned by the REST API, or written to logs.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== Help ===== -->
    <section class="jim-admin-panel" data-panel="help">
        <h3>Admin guide</h3>
        <div class="jim-admin-help">
            <h4>Global chat mode</h4>
            <p><strong>Allow everyone</strong> is the default: any active Jira user can find and message any other user.
               <strong>Restricted by policy</strong> switches to a whitelist model — a user can only search/start/receive chat when an ALLOW policy matches and no higher-priority DENY matches.
               <strong>Disabled</strong> turns chat off entirely: user search returns nothing and starting or sending direct messages is rejected by the server.</p>

            <h4>How policies are evaluated</h4>
            <ol>
                <li>Only <em>enabled</em> policies whose capability checkbox (search / start / receive) matches the action being checked are considered.</li>
                <li>The policy <em>source</em> must match the acting user (their username, user key, or a group they belong to).</li>
                <li>The policy <em>target</em> must match the other user (username/key, group, or ANY).</li>
                <li>Among matching policies the <strong>highest priority wins</strong>; on a priority tie <strong>DENY overrides ALLOW</strong>.</li>
                <li>If no policy matches, access is <strong>denied</strong> (restricted mode is a whitelist).</li>
            </ol>
            <p>Starting a chat additionally requires the recipient to be allowed to <em>receive</em> chat from the initiator. Enforcement happens in the REST API (user search, conversation creation, message send), not just the UI.</p>
            <p>Example: allow the <code>developers</code> group to chat with anyone — source <code>GROUP:developers</code>, target <code>ANY</code>, action <code>ALLOW</code>, all capabilities checked.
               Then block one user: source <code>USER:contractor1</code>, target <code>ANY</code>, action <code>DENY</code>, higher priority.</p>

            <h4>Notifications</h4>
            <p>Web push requires HTTPS and each user enabling notifications from the chat page (bell icon). The detail level controls how much content leaves the Jira server inside push payloads — use <em>Sender only</em> or <em>Generic only</em> in privacy-sensitive environments. The test button sends a push to your own browser subscriptions.</p>

            <h4>Attachments</h4>
            <p>Disabling attachments also disables voice messages (they are stored as audio attachments). The extension allowlist further restricts the built-in safe type list — it cannot enable types that are blocked for security (executables, scripts, HTML).</p>

            <h4>Diagnostics</h4>
            <p>HTTPS must be detected for web push and voice recording to work in browsers. "VAPID configured" confirms the push signing keys exist. If pushes fail after a base URL / domain change, users need to re-enable notifications once from the chat page (subscriptions are bound to the browser origin).</p>

            <h4>Audit log</h4>
            <p>Every settings change, policy change and test notification is recorded with the acting administrator, timestamp and details — see the Overview tab.</p>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
</body>
</html>
